>  Ingredients:
> - 1 lb ground beef
> - 1 packet taco seasoning (or your preferred spices)
> - 1 bag tortilla chips
> - 1 =C2=BD cups shredded cheddar or Mexican blend cheese
> - =C2=BD cup diced tomatoes
> - =C2=BD cup sliced jalape=C3=B1os (optional)
> - =C2=BD cup chopped onions (optional)
> - Sour cream, guacamole, and salsa for serving
> - Chopped cilantro for garnish (optional)
>=20
> ### Instructions:
> 1. **Cook the ground beef:**
>    - In a large skillet, cook the ground beef over medium heat until brown=
ed (about 6-8 minutes).
>    - Drain excess fat and stir in the taco seasoning along with =C2=BC cup=
 of water. Simmer for a few minutes until the seasoning is well mixed and th=
e liquid reduces.
>=20
> 2. **Assemble the nachos:**
>    - Preheat your oven to 375=C2=B0F (190=C2=B0C).
>    - On a large baking sheet or oven-safe dish, spread a layer of tortilla=
 chips.
>    - Evenly distribute the cooked ground beef over the chips.
>    - Sprinkle the shredded cheese generously on top of the beef.
>    - Add toppings like diced tomatoes, onions, and jalape=C3=B1os (if usin=
g).
>=20
> 3. **Bake:**
>    - Place the baking sheet in the oven and bake for 8-10 minutes, or unti=
l the cheese is melted and bubbly.
>=20
> 4. **Serve:**
>    - Remove from the oven and top with sour cream, guacamole, and salsa as=
 desired. Garnish with chopped cilantro if using.
>=20

